From 9da8b390425f0febbd494c15d1ba580af444eb24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:09:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09498/11362] Generalization floor gains activity 4: supervisor
 refinement from the redirect ledger

Append-only amendment to the ARC-AGI-3 Generalization-Testing Floor
(CLAUDE.md), not a new MANDATORY rule -- the 2026-08-21 coherence plan
recommends consolidation over accretion. The new qualifying activity
reads the REQ-ARC-WMTE-6640 receipts (per-arm fired/helped counts,
stagnations_unredirected) and refines the arm table by SELECTION:
retire a never-helping arm, promote a consistently-helping one, and
treat all-arms-exhausted stagnation as the written spec for a NEW arm
(arm growth stays a human/outer-loop act; a 27B cannot propose arms).

Two properties stated in the rule text:
- Prerequisite: the activity qualifies only now that the ledger carries
  outcomes; before that the task had no input and would invent work.
- Anti-churn: an empty ledger is a legitimate state; "no firings,
  nothing to refine" satisfies the slot at zero cost.

Enforcement stays WARN-only. _GENERALIZATION_SIGNALS gained
"trajectory supervisor" / "redirect ledger" / "arm_outcomes"
(task-class 4) so a compliant task counts instead of drawing a
spurious zero-qualifying-tasks warning. Mutation-proven: removing the
three signals turns test_supervisor_refinement_task_matches RED.

Both touched Python files also picked up a mechanical `ruff format`
pass: they had not been committed since the ruff v0.15.17 bump and the
pre-commit format hook (correctly) refuses them unformatted. No
semantic change in the reflowed lines.

Tests: 19 passed (test_arc_levelup_guarantee_lint.py, --no-cov).

